    (v_topic_id, 'A 84-year-old man with multiple chronic conditions, recurrent falls, and polypharmacy is referred to a Comprehensive Geriatric Assessment (CGA) program. The patient asks why he needs to see a whole team instead of just his primary care doctor. Which of the following statements best describes the evidence-based benefit and composition of the CGA interdisciplinary team?', '["CGA is a diagnostic tool performed exclusively by a neurologist to determine genetic risk profiles for dementia", "CGA is a billing code that allows multiple physicians to charge for the same office visit without collaborating", "CGA is a palliative care service designed only for patients with a life expectancy of less than 6 months", "CGA is a home safety inspection team that is legally mandated to confiscate driving licenses from patients over 80", "CGA utilizes an interdisciplinary team (geriatrician, nurse, pharmacist, social worker, PT/OT) to deliver multidimensional assessment and coordinated care, which has been shown to reduce hospital readmissions, delay nursing home placement, and improve functional survival"]'::jsonb, 4, 'A **Comprehensive Geriatric Assessment (CGA)** is a multidimensional, interdisciplinary diagnostic and therapeutic process designed to determine an older person''s medical, psychological, and functional capabilities. The core interdisciplinary team typically includes a geriatrician, nurse, clinical pharmacist, social worker, and physical/occupational therapists. Strong clinical trial evidence demonstrates that CGA-based care leads to **improved functional status, reduced rates of hospitalization and nursing home placement, and increased likelihood of remaining alive in one''s own home** compared to standard care. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 12; Ellis et al., Cochrane Database Syst Rev 2017)'),
    (v_topic_id, 'A 89-year-old woman with multiple chronic conditions, recurrent falls, and polypharmacy is referred to a Comprehensive Geriatric Assessment (CGA) program. The patient asks why she needs to see a whole team instead of just her primary care doctor. Which of the following statements best describes the evidence-based benefit and composition of the CGA interdisciplinary team?', '["CGA utilizes an interdisciplinary team (geriatrician, nurse, pharmacist, social worker, PT/OT) to deliver multidimensional assessment and coordinated care, which has been shown to reduce hospital readmissions, delay nursing home placement, and improve functional survival", "CGA is a diagnostic tool performed exclusively by a neurologist to determine genetic risk profiles for dementia", "CGA is a home safety inspection team that is legally mandated to confiscate driving licenses from patients over 80", "CGA is a palliative care service designed only for patients with a life expectancy of less than 6 months", "CGA is a billing code that allows multiple physicians to charge for the same office visit without collaborating"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A **Comprehensive Geriatric Assessment (CGA)** is a multidimensional, interdisciplinary diagnostic and therapeutic process designed to determine an older person''s medical, psychological, and functional capabilities. The core interdisciplinary team typically includes a geriatrician, nurse, clinical pharmacist, social worker, and physical/occupational therapists. Strong clinical trial evidence demonstrates that CGA-based care leads to **improved functional status, reduced rates of hospitalization and nursing home placement, and increased likelihood of remaining alive in one''s own home** compared to standard care. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 12; Ellis et al., Cochrane Database Syst Rev 2017)'),
